{"byteLength":427,"contentHash":{"algorithm":"sha256","value":"7bc07d964cec806702a816a063f7381f60e2fc805e796093327b47005eeb4b35"},"kind":"skillDocument","name":"references/stdlib/ByteOrder.md","producer":{"build":{"commit":"5de2594ad523fba4f38fa63f7a1b306e8a23eb0c","dirty":false,"provenance":{"commit":"git","dirty":"environment"},"target":"aarch64-apple-darwin"},"name":"benitoite","version":"0.0.13"},"schemaVersion":1,"text":"# Benitoite.ByteOrder\n\nStatus: standard, in the prelude. It can be used without `import`.\n\nRefer to its declarations as `ByteOrder.<name>`, for example `ByteOrder.ByteOrder`.\n\nByte orders for reading and writing integers in `Bytes`.\n\n```benitoite\npublic data ByteOrder\n  /// The most significant byte first.\n  BigEndian\n  /// The least significant byte first.\n  LittleEndian\nend data\n```\n\nThe order of the bytes of an integer.\n"}
